<!--
    Swift name demangling.

    Issue: a Swift binary renders its symbols as mangled soup. On a large third-party
    iOS app (84 MB arm64, Swift + Objective-C) kuna printed the imported
    `$sSo9OS_os_logC0B0E9subsystem8categoryABSS_SStcfC` and, with the ObjC
    metadata pass on, Swift classes under their runtime names
    (`-[_TtC6Sample24MainScreenViewController viewDidLoad]`). The earlier
    name-only subset demangled 26% of the Swift symbols; the demangler now
    reads the whole stable grammar (`$s`) and the ObjC runtime type names
    (`_Tt`) and demangles all of them.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 environment-binding, the loader's symbol-name
    demangle seam (`kuna-analysis/src/analyzers/demangle/kuna_swift.rs`,
    reached from `demangle_name` while the symbol table is installed) and the
    ObjC metadata pass's class-name rendering (`analyzers/objc/mod.rs`).

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture. The pass clears
    it and loads the real arm64 Mach-O fixture `macho_swift_names_arm64`
    (built from `macho_swift_names.m`, see the fixtures README): an
    Objective-C root class whose runtime name is the Swift form
    `_TtC4main7Greeter` (what swiftc emits for `@objc class Greeter` in
    module `main`), and an exported function under the Swift 5 symbol
    `_$s4main10countWords2ofS2i_tF` (`main.countWords(of: Swift.Int) ->
    Swift.Int`). The ObjC pass is on so the class name reaches the method
    label.

    The function is `main.countWords(of:)` and the method
    `-[main.Greeter greet:]`, where the mangled soup read
    `$s4main10countWords2ofS2i_tF` and `-[_TtC4main7Greeter greet:]`.
    `self` is the class's own instance struct (`objcivars`), which keeps the
    runtime name `_TtC4main7Greeter`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_swift_names_arm64</com>
  <com>option objc on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x1000005fc</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load addr 0x1000005f0</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="swiftdemangle: the Swift 5 symbol never stays mangled" min="0" max="0">\$s4main10countWords2ofS2i_tF\(int4 a0\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="swiftdemangle: the ObjC method label never carries the runtime class name" min="0" max="0">-\[_TtC4main7Greeter greet:\]\(_TtC4main7Greeter \*self</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="swiftdemangle: the Swift 5 symbol demangles to its reference path" min="1" max="1">main\.countWords\(of:\)\(int4 a0\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="swiftdemangle: the ObjC method label carries the demangled class name" min="1" max="1">-\[main\.Greeter greet:\]\(_TtC4main7Greeter \*self</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="the function body is kept" min="1" max="1">return a0 &lt;&lt; 1 \| 1;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="the method body is kept" min="1" max="1">return arg1 \* 3 \+ 7;</stringmatch>
